// A `const` item has NO static storage. Logos has no const-eval by design
// (project_no_const_eval): a const is name + type + lowered expression, and
// mlir_gen materialises that expression INTO THE FRAME at every use. So `&K`
// borrows frame storage exactly as `&local` does, and returning it dangles.
//
// MEASURED before the refusal, with the clobber constant varied so a lucky
// stable read could not pass for a correct one: this program returned 71 and 9
// where 5 is correct. The `static` twin — one llvm.mlir.global, stable address
// — is CORRECT and stays admitted: pass/bc_static_item_return_ref_admit.
//
// Not the operator-temporary case closed at 7518f318: `const K: i64 = 2i64 +
// 3i64;` behaves identically, because the const's expression is not inlined at
// the borrow site. The borrow arrives as an AddrOf naming "K", not an
// AddrOfTemp, so no widening of is_temporary_value_expr reaches it.
package bc_const_item_return_ref_fail;

const K: i64 = 5i64;

fn f() -> &i64 { return &K; }

fn main() -> i64 { let r: &i64 = f(); return *r; }
